#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#616 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 2: This is Charleston 3."
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#617 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 1: Equipped with a heavy weapon, this combat unit is capable of both offense and defense."
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#618 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 1: It has a pilot cockpit inside, and armed with thick plates that can withstand most explosions."
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#619 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 1: To turn it on, push the lever to the center and press the power switch."
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#620 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 2: That's not even in the main computer's database. How did you know that?"
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#621 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 1: That's not important. Whoever gets in her wins, right? I won."
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#622 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 2: ...!"
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#623 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 1: Hey, did you have to push me?!"
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#624 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 2: Push the lever to the center and press the power switch."
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#625 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 2: I'm destroying everything, so no more sad robots like me will ever see the world."
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#626 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 2: My laser beam will liberate all the robots from their misery!"
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#627 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 1: I'm not capable of combat. I can't stop you."
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#628 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 2: So stop following me. I really can destroy you if I want to!"
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#629 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 1: I've brought some people who can help you."
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#630 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 2: I thought humans could not enter the Core."
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#631 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 1: Hm, I think you're right."
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#632 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 1: This may not be useful in combat, but I've learned from a pretty lady how to scream."
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#633 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 2: Why didn't you learn something more useful in combat?"
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#634 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 1: Didn't have a choice."
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#635 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 2: Stop me and suffer the consequences. I can always replace you, you know."
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#636 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 1: The next model may or may not be like you and me. It doesn't matter. You have to be stopped."
